-- `hub` re-exports two unrelated `mth : a -> a`, from `IA` (`n + 1`) and `IB`
-- (`n * 10`), both with an impl at `Int`.  Inside `wrap` the receiver is the rigid
-- `x`, which no declaration's impl query can be asked about, and `wrap` declares no
-- constraint, so the two declarations are not shown to agree.  SHADOW-SEMANTICS.md
-- S2-DECL (d) over the admitted set (ruled 2026-10-14): the located reject
-- `T-AMBIGUOUS-METHOD` at `mth` in `wrap`, exit 1 on every verb, in either hub order
-- (`swapped.mdk`).  Never 4 or 30, which the two hub orders printed while the
-- occurrence kept no route.
import hub.{IA, IB, mth}

wrap : x -> x
wrap v = mth v

main = println (wrap (3 : Int))
